---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SubmitForm from '../../components/SubmitForm.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Report a problem"
  description="Something wrong in an entry? Tell us what it is. A person reads every report."
>
  <h1>Report a problem</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Wrong, out of date, misleading, or explained in a way that does not land. All four are worth
    reporting, and the fourth one is the hardest to spot from the inside.
  </p>

  <SubmitForm kind="fix" />

  <h2>What Happens Next</h2>
  <p>
    A person reads it and checks it. If you are right, the entry changes and the correction goes live
    with the next deploy. If you are wrong, or if it is more arguable than it looks, that is useful too:
    an entry that two people read differently is usually an entry that needs rewriting whoever turns out
    to be correct.
  </p>
  <p>
    Corrections get the same credit line as suggestions if you leave a name.
  </p>
</Base>
